  "id": "Compound::DB00334 - Gene::152",
  "verbalization": "Olanzapine is implicated in the interaction with Adra2c through a mechanism involving the Alpha-adrenergic Receptor Activity. The evidence suggests that Olanzapine binds to Adra1a and Adra2a, which are both involved in the same biological process—Alpha-adrenergic Receptor Activity. This activity is then recognized by Adra2c, indicating a potential functional link between Olanzapine and Adra2c. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Olanzapine in modulating the activity of Adra2c, though the exact mechanism of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence from both paths supports a shared pathway involving Alpha-adrenergic receptors, suggesting that Olanzapine may influence Adra2c through a common regulatory mechanism.",
